From 089450dd1804b16b558b3d256076e4dd12d25ded Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duckfamily <156525766+duckfamily@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Aug 2026 02:33:38 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 08/13] Rotate proxies when media stalls, and expose the state

A proxy can carry the main datacentre perfectly while refusing the file
datacentres, so messages arrive and photos never load. Rotation never
noticed, because it only looked at mtp().dcstate() - the main datacentre -
and stopped the moment that was connected.

The signal used instead is restartsByTimeout() filtered to download
datacentres, which is upstream's own definition of a stalled download. Three
inside twenty-five seconds means the proxy, not the file. The offender is
skipped for ten minutes and the quickest responding candidate takes over.
If every candidate has failed on media the history is cleared rather than
leaving someone stranded on a proxy that cannot load a photo.

Also adds snapshots, a change stream, switch history with reasons and a
stall counter, so the connection dashboard has something to read. probeAll()
measures without switching: moving someone off a working proxy because they
opened a page would be rude.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
